@startuml
title TMFC030 : Bill Generation Management -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

class "Create Customer Bill Invoice L3" as CreateCustomerBillInvoice <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "Produce & Distribute Customer Bill L3" as ProduceDistributeCustomerBill <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "BP Bill/Invoice Control L3" as BPBillInvoiceControl <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "BP Bill/Invoice Lifecycle Management L3" as BPBillInvoiceLifecycleManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "Customer Bill" as CustomerBill <<SID Data Entity>>
class "Party Bill" as PartyBill <<SID Data Entity>>

' Each of these four pairs is drawn in the image as a single double-headed
' arrow between an eTOM activity and a SID ABE. Per the image's own legend,
' an arrow from the eTOM activity towards the SID ABE means information
' produced by the activity; the reverse arrow means information consumed by
' the activity -- both hold simultaneously for a double-headed arrow.
CreateCustomerBillInvoice --> CustomerBill : produces
CustomerBill --> CreateCustomerBillInvoice : is consumed by

ProduceDistributeCustomerBill --> CustomerBill : produces
CustomerBill --> ProduceDistributeCustomerBill : is consumed by

BPBillInvoiceControl --> PartyBill : produces
PartyBill --> BPBillInvoiceControl : is consumed by

BPBillInvoiceLifecycleManagement --> PartyBill : produces
PartyBill --> BPBillInvoiceLifecycleManagement : is consumed by

' Cross-link: a single-headed curved arrow, distinct from the four pairs
' above, running from the Party Bill<->BP Bill/Invoice Control line up to a
' second, separate arrowhead on "Create Customer Bill Invoice L3" (confirmed
' by cropping and zooming into the arrowhead region at 4-6x -- the curve
' carries its own thin arrowhead into the activity box, and only branches,
' without an arrowhead, off the Party Bill line). This is still an
' eTOM-activity <-> SID-ABE arrow, so the legend's meaning applies: an arrow
' into the activity means the information is consumed by it.
PartyBill --> CreateCustomerBillInvoice : is consumed by

note bottom of CustomerBill
  *insert notes if needed
end note

legend right
  eTOM Business Activity = dashed-outline rectangle (source image)
  SID Data Entities = cylinders
  arrow eTOM -> SID = information produced by the activity
  arrow SID -> eTOM = information consumed by the activity
endlegend
@enduml
